{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>נגש.</b> From the nif'al binyan." "<b>ולא יפתח פיו.</b> There is no need to interpret this, for every Jew is so in exile: when he is tormented he does not open his mouth to speak. All the more so the righteous among them does not involve himself in his world but only in the service of HaShem, and does not recognize any officer or great man to stand in the breach for him when a person rises against him, nor does he open (for him) his mouth — and the meaning is at all times."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 53, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:59:20.515110750Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}